    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0906.3146v1</id>
    <title>Lambda-rings and the field with one element</title>
    <updated>2009-06-17T11:27:20Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.3146v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0906.3146v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  The theory of Lambda-rings, in the sense of Grothendieck's Riemann-Roch theory, is an enrichment of the theory of commutative rings. In the same way, we can enrich usual algebraic geometry over the ring Z of integers to produce Lambda-algebraic geometry. We show that Lambda-algebraic geometry is in a precise sense an algebraic geometry over a deeper base than Z and that it has many properties predicted for algebraic geometry over the mythical field with one element. Moreover, it does this is a way that is both formally robust and closely related to active areas in arithmetic algebraic geometry.</summary>
